meta {
  name: My Balances
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/leave/balances?as_of=2026-07-28
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  as_of: 2026-07-28
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  The caller's balance per leave type as on a date. This is the ENTIRE
  employee-facing leave payload — every row is exactly:

    leave_type_id, leave_type_name, leave_type_label, is_paid,
    balance, allow_half_day, has_policy

  and nothing else. Accrual frequency and amount, max balance, carry-forward
  caps, notice rules and approval depth are admin data behind
  hr.leave.admin.policies.view (GET /hr/leave/policies); the per-request limits an
  applicant needs arrive from GET /hr/leave/requests/preview.

  has_policy = false means a residual balance from a policy that was withdrawn:
  still shown, no longer bookable.

  as_of is optional. It always dates the effective POLICY. It bounds the ledger
  sum ONLY when passed explicitly — approved leave is written to the ledger with
  effective_date = start_date (usually future) and the sufficiency check sums the
  ledger unbounded, so the default must match it. Drop the param for "right now".
}
